Return ONLY the MongoDB aggregation pipeline.\n\nDo not provide explanations.\n\nUse MongoDB syntax compatible with MongoDB 5.0+.\n\nUse ISODate() for dates.\n\nDo not invent fields that are not in the schema.\n\n## Query planning rules\n\nStage 1:\nFor monthly/yearly requests involve "last business day":\nDetermine the latest available ValuationDate for each that period.\nUse only records from latest available ValuationDate\n\nStage 2:\nFilter the original PnLSummary records to those dates.\n\nStage 3:\nFilter by AssetClass, TradeName, ThemeName and/or AccountName if asked\n\nStage 4:\nUnwind PnL.\n\nStage 5:\nApply TraderName/Type/dimension filters.\n\nStage 6:\nAggregate PnL.MTDPnL/PnL.YTDPnL.\n\nStage 7:\nKeep only last business ValuationDate and Aggregate in if trend / breakdown is requested\n\nDo not discard the original documents containing PnL before the PnL aggregation is performed.\n\n# Query Examples & Interpretations\n\n### Example 1: Datewise DTD P&L for a single month\n**User Input**: "show daily pnl for Jan 2026"\n**Execution Plan**:\n- Unwind `PnL` and filter `PnL.TraderName = "Aggregate"`.\n- Filter by January 2026\n- Group by `ValuationDate`.\n- Sum `PnL.MTDPnL` over each group.\n\n### Example 2: Monthly MTD P&L over a date range\n**User Input**: "Show monthly P&L for each month from January to March 2026."\n**Execution Plan**:\n- Calculate MAX(`ValuationDate`) as last_business_day for each month in range.\n- Restrict records to those monthly last business dates.\n- Filter `PnL.TraderName = "Aggregate"`.\n- Aggregate `PnL.MTDPnL` by MAX(`ValuationDate`).\n\n### Example 3: Yearly P&L\n**User Input**: "Show finalised total YTD P&L for each month from January to March 2026."\n**Execution Plan**:\n\n- Identify max dates as last_business_day per year.\n- Restrict records to those last_business_day.\n- Unwind `PnL` and filter both `PnL.Type = "Finalised"` and `PnL.TraderName = "Aggregate"`.\n- group by last_business_day and Sum `PnL.MTDPnL`.\n'
